--
Header-free cvise reduction (/tmp/r163/red/kb_U6c, from libc++ 18's
views::take(3), signature: the drop of take's operator()) of test.desc.
Fixed in steps: round 163v (the trailing return type
`decltype(__bind_back_t<...>(forward_as_tuple(__args...)))' resolves) and
round 163w: N5008 [temp.inst]/4, [basic.def.odr]/5 -- that decltype
selects the inherited constructor template of __perfect_forward_impl,
whose specialization is not odr-used there; its body (ill-formed for the
declared `tuple<> forward_as_tuple(int)' of the reduction) was
instantiated and dropped ("found no match for symbol '__tuple_impl'").  A
member function template specialization instantiated in an unevaluated
operand during an instantiation is now held back (speculative_instances)
like a function template's.  clang++ 18 accepts the program (it uses
clang's __make_integer_seq and __type_pack_element builtins, which g++
does not have).  Pre-existing (fails on bin53).
